summary:
Heard this year's @icmlconf passed submission number 4600 by the abstract submission deadline. Based on #NeurIPS2018's number-to-submission ratio ( a very (very!) rough est is ~2800 "real" submissions. This is vs last year's 2500 submissions #ICML2019 1/2
Quoting @hugo_larochelle
@hoonoseme @NipsConference No it’s more like 4900 for 2018... these numbers from past years don’t include withdrawn papers. A lot of submissions are withdrawn prior to the deadline, for various reasons.

Thoughtful debate must begin with accurate facts. At @icmlconf there is gentle encouragement, but no "demand" for code, and no requirement whatsoever about data. See our FAQ:
Quoting @NandoDF
@ilyasut It is also surprising that conferences like @icmlconf and @iclr2019 are increasingly demanding code and dataset releases despite authors pointing out potential unethical uses of their datasets. We need thoughtful debate at upcoming conferences, and responsible solutions.

